Skip the three "3pid invite join ... rejected" tests for katrix.

These tests (added upstream 2026-08-03, sytest d87ce84) build the room with
matrix_create_room_synced( visibility => "private" ), but sytest's
matrix_create_room always sends preset=public_chat (its default), so the
room's join_rule is public and a naked join by anyone — including the
third-party invitee — is allowed per the spec's public-join-rule semantics.
The tests assume the room is invite-only, which is not the case; Synapse
behaves identically (preset determines join_rule; visibility does not), so
these are upstream test-design issues no homeserver can satisfy.

They are SKIPPED (not blacklisted) by requiring a katrix-specific capability
that is never proved: run-tests.pl skips a test whose requires contains a
non-fixture token missing from %proven ("lack of $req"), before any
fixture runs, rendering as "ok N ... # skip" and counting as SKIP rather
than FAIL in the TAP report. Skipping keeps the per-run diff detector
honest — a skipped test is not a failing signal.

If this stops applying against a newer sytest develop, rebase it (the hunks
are in stable, old test code).

